# =====================================================================
# SC4UIScale — ALLOWLIST .gitignore
#
# ⛔ THIS FILE IS AN ALLOWLIST, NOT A DENYLIST, AND THAT IS DELIBERATE.
# Task #108 measured the excluded:shipped ratio in this tree at ~200:1.
# At that ratio a denylist ships a leak the first time someone adds a
# directory nobody thought about. So: ignore EVERYTHING, then re-include
# only what is named. A new directory is invisible until someone adds it
# here on purpose.
#
# Policy: ship the GENERATOR, never the art.
#   (a) no PII — usernames, machine paths, OneDrive layout
#   (b) nothing derived from the game install (EA/Maxis)
#   (c) nothing from other modders (CAM, warrior, CoriBoom, memo33, …)
#       EXCEPT the gzcom-dll and MinHook git submodules under vendor/
#   (d) no screenshots, no logs, no build output, no session state
#
# The player's own game install supplies the art. See RUNBOOK.md §1.
# =====================================================================

# ---- 1. ignore everything ------------------------------------------
/*

# ---- 2. re-include the tracked trees -------------------------------
!/.gitignore
!/HANDOFF-2026-08-23.md
!/HANDOFF-2026-08-25-carbon.md
!/src/
!/vendor/
!/docs/
!/tools/
!/_packaging/
!/_tests/

# ---- 3. re-include root documents ----------------------------------
!/README.md
!/CONTINUITY.md
!/RUNBOOK.md
!/CHANGELOG.md
!/START-HERE.md
!/LICENSE
!/NOTICE
!/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md
!/VERSION-HISTORY.txt

# ---- 4. re-exclude bulk INSIDE the tracked trees --------------------
# Everything below is regenerable from the game install or from source.
# If you find yourself wanting to commit one of these, the answer is
# almost always to commit the SCRIPT that makes it instead.

# game-derived art, extracted or scaled
/tools/dbpf/extracted*/
/tools/upscale/preview*/
/tools/upscale/test/
/tools/selective-safe/stage*/
/tools/selective-safe/superseded/
/tools/itemicons/nam-*/
/tools/itemicons/out/
/tools/itemicons/stage*/
/tools/uiscripts/extracted*/
/tools/selective/
/tools/capture/out/

# built archives and binaries (regenerated by the builders)
*.dat
*.exe
*.dll
*.pdb
*.lib
*.exp
*.obj
*.pyc
__pycache__/

# session state, logs, captures, goldens
/_tests/captures/
/_tests/golden/*.png
/_tests/*.log
*.log

# large derived analysis output (the .py that makes it IS tracked)
/tools/uimap/_work/
/tools/uimap/diff/
/tools/research/**/*.tsv
/tools/research/**/*.pkl
/tools/research/**/*.png
/tools/research/**/*.sc4

# ---- 5. re-include small derived lists the builders READ ------------
# These are inputs, not outputs — a cold clone needs them.
!/tools/upscale/*.txt
!/tools/selective-safe/package-list*.txt
!/tools/itemicons/_work/item_icons_distinct.txt
!/tools/fonts/*.ini
!/tools/uiscripts/winning-corpus.json
!/tools/research/udriveit/clsid-name-table.json

# ---- 6. never, under any circumstances ------------------------------
/dist/
/build/
/_working-backup/
/_archive/
/_HANDOFF-SimCity4-Complete/
/_vanilla-reference/


# ---- 7. noisy directories: allowlist per FILE, not per tree ---------
# Measured 2026-08-18: a bare `!/tools/` admitted 4,662 files from
# itemicons alone (per-icon extract-manifest.csv / SOURCE.txt cache
# stubs) and 915 from dialog-static staging. Ship the builders and the
# reports; never the cache.
/tools/itemicons/*
!/tools/itemicons/*.py
!/tools/itemicons/*.md
!/tools/itemicons/_work/
/tools/itemicons/_work/*
!/tools/itemicons/_work/item_icons_distinct.txt
# The 130 canonical names of the user-confirmed 2x Sub package. It is OUR
# derived list, not anyone's art, and build_itemicons_sub.py checks the tier
# set against it. Without this a cold clone has no reference and cannot tell a
# correct package from one silently short an icon.
!/tools/itemicons/_work/pack-sub-manifest.txt

/tools/dialog-static/*
!/tools/dialog-static/*.py
!/tools/dialog-static/*.md
# thirdparty-src\ holds another mod's .UI scripts - never committed. The
# README beside them is OURS and is the only record of why that folder exists,
# what each script is, and how to re-derive it. Exclude the CONTENTS, not the
# directory: git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded,
# and `/tools/dialog-static/*` above already excluded this one - so re-admit
# the DIRECTORY first, then shut its contents, then name the one exception.
!/tools/dialog-static/thirdparty-src/
/tools/dialog-static/thirdparty-src/*
!/tools/dialog-static/thirdparty-src/README.md
/tools/dialog-static/thirdparty-art/

/tools/oddballs/*
!/tools/oddballs/*.cs
!/tools/oddballs/*.md
!/tools/oddballs/*.csv

/tools/uimap/*
!/tools/uimap/*.py
!/tools/uimap/*.md
!/tools/uimap/emu/
/tools/uimap/emu/*
!/tools/uimap/emu/*.py

/_tests/repro166/
/_packaging/public-repo/

# policy (d): no screenshots, anywhere under _tests
/_tests/**/*.png
/_tests/**/*.jpg

# tools/dbpf holds EXTRACTED GAME ART in several sibling dirs
# (intro-extract, intro-src, intro-up-*). Ship only the tooling.
/tools/dbpf/*
!/tools/dbpf/*.cs
!/tools/dbpf/*.py
!/tools/dbpf/*.md

# policy (d) globally: this repo carries NO images. Art comes from the
# game install; screenshots are session state. No exceptions.
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.bmp
*.fsh

# research/ holds ONLY the distilled laws + index. The full corpus lives
# at its real paths (tools/research, _tests) now that the working tree IS
# the repo - mirroring it under research/ would be two copies drifting.
!/research/

# ---- #200 sharpness investigation scratch (2026-08-29) --------------------
# The 1.5x sharpness lanes left ~9,900 throwaway measurement scripts AND
# EXTRACTED GAME ART (.bin payloads pulled from shipped dats) under
# tools/research/sharp15/. Policy (b): nothing derived from the game install
# ever enters this repo. Keep ONLY the derivation tool whose output ships -
# the measurements are reproducible from it, the art is not ours to carry.
/tools/research/sharp15/*
!/tools/research/sharp15/make_even_strips.py
